# Example Caddy config for prodbox. Caddy is the only thing facing the internet: the
# container port is bound to 127.0.0.1, and Caddy runs on the host (not inside
# docker/deploy/compose.deploy.yml), terminating TLS and reverse-proxying to the
# loopback port this stack's container published.
#
# Copy to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile (or fold into an existing one alongside the canonry
# product repository's own Caddyfile - the two are independent, unrelated blocks),
# replace the domain, reload Caddy.
#
# Two isolated stacks live on this box, prod and preview, each with its own subdomain
# and its own container on a different loopback port (5195 prod, 5295 preview - see
# docker/deploy/secrets.env.example). Both DNS records must be grey-clouded
# (Cloudflare: DNS-only, proxy switch off) rather than orange-clouded, or Caddy cannot
# complete its own ACME challenge and terminate TLS directly:
#
#   canonry.io          A/AAAA  <prodbox IP>   ; prod, grey-clouded
#   preview.canonry.io   A/AAAA  <prodbox IP>   ; preview, grey-clouded

canonry.io {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5195
}

# Preview stack: same shape, its own compose project and its own port.
# preview.canonry.io {
# 	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5295
# }
